1
00:00:16,590 --> 00:00:19,550
I have some suggestions to help you improve

2
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:20,570
your listening scores.

3
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:24,470
Firstly, you should do listening exercises with increasing

4
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:25,050
difficulty.

5
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,690
You should start with easy ones, such as

6
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:32,150
sentence completion and short answer questions, and remember

7
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:33,830
to practice each of them carefully.

8
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:37,630
After finishing, you should analyze which question you

9
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:41,630
answer incorrectly, why you make those mistakes, find

10
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:43,150
and learn new vocabulary.

11
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:46,410
Our goal is to increase the percentage of

12
00:00:46,410 --> 00:00:48,430
correct answers to 80%.

13
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:50,450
By doing that, you will be less pressured

14
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,430
when practicing other question types.

15
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:55,350
If you haven't mastered the easy exercises yet,

16
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:57,470
it's likely that you will give up difficult

17
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:57,830
ones.

18
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:00,750
In the next phase, you will practice more

19
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:01,870
difficult question types.

20
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:04,489
They are summary completion.

21
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:07,190
For this one, you have to listen for

22
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:08,030
many synonyms.

23
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:11,270
If you don't know the synonyms of words,

24
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:13,610
it's likely that you can't find the answers.

25
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:18,150
The next one is flowchart, and then map

26
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:18,750
completion.

27
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:23,650
These question types assess your sensitivity and reflexes

28
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:24,610
when you listen.

29
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:27,930
For example, if you haven't identified the east

30
00:01:27,930 --> 00:01:30,490
-north direction on the map while the speaker

31
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,570
is talking about it, how can you find

32
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:33,170
the answers?

33
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:36,970
Other question types you can practice are matching

34
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:38,930
or multiple-choice questions.

35
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:41,510
You need to choose the correct answer from

36
00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:42,970
a wide range of options.

37
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:45,230
When all the options are mentioned by the

38
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:47,310
speaker, which answer would you choose?

39
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:50,350
Just by hearing the keywords, it's really difficult

40
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:51,710
to choose the correct one.

41
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:55,030
So, when practicing these types, please follow all

42
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:57,310
the steps I introduced to you so that

43
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:58,990
you can get your desired scores.
